(CODELENS KNOWLEDGE BASE - DATABASE CONNECTIONS & CONTEXT MANAGERS \(PAGE 1\)) '
(================================================================================) '
(Module: Database Connection Pooling and Resource Safety Guide) '
() '
(1. DATABASE CONNECTION LEAKS IN BACKEND SERVICES) '
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) '
(A common critical issue in backend services is failing to close database connections.) '
(When a connection is opened via db.connect\(\) without a context manager, any runtime) '
(exception in subsequent queries causes the connection to remain open indefinitely.) '
() '
(Symptom: OperationalError: Too many connections / connection pool exhaustion.) '
() '
(Problematic Pattern:) '
(    conn = db_pool.get_connection\(\)) '
(    cursor = conn.cursor\(\)) '
(    cursor.execute\('SELECT * FROM users WHERE active = 1'\)) '
(    records = cursor.fetchall\(\)) '
(    # If an error happens above, conn.close\(\) is never reached!) '
(    conn.close\(\)) '
() '
(2. SAFE RESOURCE RECOVERY USING CONTEXT MANAGERS) '
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) '
(In Python, always manage connections using the 'with' statement or try-finally blocks.) '
(The context manager guarantees that the __exit__ method executes conn.close\(\) or) '
(returns the connection back to the connection pool, even if an exception is raised.) '
ET
endstream
endobj
