(CODELENS KNOWLEDGE BASE - DATABASE CONNECTIONS & CONTEXT MANAGERS \(PAGE 2\)) '
(================================================================================) '
(Module: Recommended Database Cleanup Idioms and Best Practices) '
() '
(3. THE RECOMMENDED CONNECTION CONTEXT MANAGER PATTERN) '
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) '
(Standard production idiom for leak-proof database transactions:) '
() '
(    with db_pool.get_connection\(\) as conn:) '
(        with conn.cursor\(\) as cursor:) '
(            cursor.execute\('SELECT * FROM users WHERE active = 1'\)) '
(            records = cursor.fetchall\(\)) '
() '
(4. EXPLICIT CLEANUP WITH TRY-FINALLY BLOCKS) '
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) '
(If a context manager is not supported by the driver, use try-finally:) '
(    conn = db_pool.get_connection\(\)) '
(    try:) '
(        cursor = conn.cursor\(\)) '
(        cursor.execute\(query\)) '
(        return cursor.fetchall\(\)) '
(    finally:) '
(        conn.close\(\)  # Guaranteed execution prevents connection leaks) '
() '
(5. RULE FOR CODE REVIEWS: Never open raw I/O or network connections without 'with'.) '
ET
endstream
endobj
